4
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:23,580
There's an expectation that this session today will give you everything you need to know

5
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:28,980
from A to Z as it relates to student life, as it relates to RSOs.

6
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:31,580
This is not the session.

7
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:39,020
However, with this session, what I hope to do, what I hope to accomplish for this session

8
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:44,180
is rather to give you a very broad overview of the policies and procedures, sharing with

9
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:51,180
you any new policies and procedures that have arisen as of last semester.

10
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:53,180
So stay tuned.

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:01:08,750
I hope this session for you is very informative and it should last about 20 to 25 minutes.

12
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:15,830
This will be a classroom full of students, advisors, officers, leaders, etc.

13
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:23,990
However, this first slide, I would like for you to give your name, your organization,

14
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:28,990
what your role is, and a very brief description of your organization.

15
00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:31,510
Again, my name is Dee Lindsey.

16
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:34,510
I'm representing the Office of Student Life as a Director.

17
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:45,560
Today we're going to talk about some of the benefits for the RSOs.

18
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:50,840
Specifically, you will have the opportunity as a recognized student organization to book

19
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:56,120
space on your particular campus completely free of charge.

20
00:01:56,120 --> 00:02:02,120
You will receive an automatic invitation to Club Rush in the fall and in the spring.

21
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:07,120
And you will also have the opportunity to open an agency account.

22
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:11,120
I have to give you a word of caution here about agency accounts.

23
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:17,120
As much as I love my own particular financial institution, for recognized student organizations,

24
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:21,120
there can be no outside bank accounts.

25
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:27,120
No Robbins Federal, no Bank of America, no BB&T, etc., etc.

26
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:35,120
I also want to make sure that everyone understands that when you fund rates, all deposits must

27
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:41,550
be deposited directly into your agency account.

28
00:02:41,550 --> 00:02:48,550
Another benefit is you have the opportunity to be nominated at our spring leadership awards,

29
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:50,550
which will be held in the spring.

30
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:54,550
You will also be eligible for co-op funding.

31
00:02:54,550 --> 00:03:03,550
And additionally, you will have the opportunity to obtain free consultation on major event planning

32
00:03:03,550 --> 00:03:05,550
and implementation.

33
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:15,550
Our conversation today will focus on organizational structure, financial management, and event

34
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:17,550
programming and planning.

35
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:23,380
Registering your student organizations.

36
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:28,380
You must register every year to be a recognized student organization.

37
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:33,380
What does registration actually mean?

38
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:37,380
That means attending training, much like you're doing today.

39
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:43,380
That means submitting your recognition documents, which includes your advisor intent form.

40
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:49,380
It also includes your drug and alcohol free campus forms, your roster, and information

41
00:03:49,380 --> 00:03:52,380
about your agency account.

42
00:03:52,380 --> 00:04:00,780
Registration, or re-registration as it were, begins with the first day of the fall semester

43
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:04,780
and ends the last business day in September.

44
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:10,780
For the spring semester, recognition or registration begins the first day of the spring semester

45
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:15,780
and ends the last business day in February.

46
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:22,780
It is important to understand that this recognition process is important for a number of reasons

47
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:23,780
for me.

48
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:29,780
It allows me to build my distribution list, thereby communicating with each of you all

49
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:35,780
on a regular basis about upcoming events in student life, student affairs, and business

50
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:36,780
of the college.

51
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:42,780
Once I have all of those forms together, I will delete my current distribution list,

52
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:48,780
pick up all of you all, add you to my new distribution list, and I will be able to have

53
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:53,780
regular communications with you as it relates to, again, student life business.

54
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:59,310
Talk about transition for just a moment.

55
00:04:59,310 --> 00:05:02,310
Why should organizations transition?

56
00:05:02,310 --> 00:05:04,310
There are a couple of good reasons why.

57
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:11,310
You can, when you transition, transfer that significant organizational knowledge.

58
00:05:11,310 --> 00:05:18,310
You can help your incoming leadership by absorbing the special expertise of your outgoing leadership.

59
00:05:18,310 --> 00:05:20,310
How can you transition?

60
00:05:20,310 --> 00:05:22,310
A couple of ways.

61
00:05:22,310 --> 00:05:24,310
You can do it by training.

62
00:05:24,310 --> 00:05:27,310
In-house training for your particular RSL.

63
00:05:27,310 --> 00:05:31,310
You can also do it by just simply observing your current officers.

64
00:05:31,310 --> 00:05:35,310
You can plan a retreat for your recognized student organization.

65
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:40,310
Or, my personal favorite, you can begin to assemble a transition notebook.

66
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:43,310
In student life, we've done just that.

67
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:49,310
Across all five campuses, we now have transition notebooks in place that kind of gives

68
00:05:49,310 --> 00:05:55,310
a very broad overview of what each person who is a student life professional,

69
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:57,310
what their job entails.

70
00:05:58,310 --> 00:06:03,310
For instance, a little while ago, the Office of Student Life suffered

71
00:06:03,310 --> 00:06:08,310
two major exits due to employee transitions.

72
00:06:08,310 --> 00:06:13,310
Before the two employees left, I worked with them to actually put together

73
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:17,310
their transition notebook, which has now been very instrumental

74
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:23,310
for the new employees to kind of see very broadly what the position actually entails.

75
00:06:26,710 --> 00:06:30,710
Earlier, I talked about the availability of space for RSOs.

76
00:06:30,710 --> 00:06:34,710
I'm going to talk about what particular locations are available

77
00:06:34,710 --> 00:06:37,710
on your respective campus.

78
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:44,710
For instance, Macon, Confront, Dublin, East Memorial, and Robbins.

79
00:06:44,710 --> 00:06:49,710
There are very critical folks in place there who can help you determine

80
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:53,710
the best location for your RSO.

81
00:06:53,710 --> 00:06:57,710
Those persons who will be your points of contact are actually

82
00:06:57,710 --> 00:07:01,710
the people who are running this particular RSO session.

83
00:07:01,710 --> 00:07:05,710
So, the key to getting some of that prime real estate on your

84
00:07:05,710 --> 00:07:08,710
respective campuses is to book early.

85
00:07:08,710 --> 00:07:12,710
I'll give you one example of booking early.

86
00:07:12,710 --> 00:07:17,710
The Macon-based Accounting Association holds a

87
00:07:17,710 --> 00:07:21,710
meet the firm night every fall.

88
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:25,710
I think it's actually in September.

89
00:07:25,710 --> 00:07:31,710
So, rather than wait until the end of August, beginning of August,

90
00:07:31,710 --> 00:07:34,710
they actually book the space in the summer.

91
00:07:34,710 --> 00:07:38,710
So, they have three or four months to decide on their date,

92
00:07:38,710 --> 00:07:44,710
get it approved, get it confirmed, on the calendar, etc., etc.

93
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:48,710
But again, the key is to book early.

94
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:52,820
Revenue producing events.

95
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:55,820
What are revenue producing events?

96
00:07:55,820 --> 00:08:01,820
Those are events that you trade a good or a service in exchange

97
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:06,820
for cash, in exchange for dollars for your particular RSO.

98
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:11,820
Revenue producing projects include the selling of t-shirts,

99
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:16,820
the selling of tickets, and or charging admission to public

100
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:21,820
activities or events, and the selling of other goods and services.

101
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:26,820
Before you fundraise, you must have an agency account on file

102
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:28,820
with the business office.

103
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:31,820
Again, you cannot have an off-campus bank account.

104
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:35,820
If you would like to establish an agency account,

105
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:46,820
please visit the following website, www.mga.com.

106
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:50,820
Once you complete the form, and I will show you what the

107
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:51,820
form looks like.

108
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:54,820
Once you complete the form, that goes to the Vice President

109
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:59,650
of Student Affairs, Ms. Jennifer Brainer.

110
00:08:59,650 --> 00:09:03,650
I also would like to say that the business office will handle

111
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:07,650
the paperwork for your particular agency account.

112
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:13,650
Student Life has nothing whatsoever to do with the agency accounts.

113
00:09:13,650 --> 00:09:16,650
I cannot give you an account balance.

114
00:09:16,650 --> 00:09:18,650
I cannot accept deposits.

115
00:09:18,650 --> 00:09:21,650
I cannot accept check requests.

116
00:09:21,650 --> 00:09:28,180
These functions must be conducted through the business office.

117
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:30,180
This is a sample.

