00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:55,180
So, in case you can't see it, this is a copy of the

126
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,180
agency account agreement form.

127
00:09:57,180 --> 00:10:01,180
Again, this will go through the Vice President of Student Affairs.

128
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:06,620
If you would like to request a balance from the business office

129
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:09,620
for your particular agency account,

130
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:13,620
please, please, please, upon the request of the business office,

131
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:17,620
refrain from using the balance inquiry request form

132
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:20,620
more than once per semester.

133
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:24,620
Maintaining your account balance is actually

134
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,620
the responsibility of your treasurer.

135
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:31,620
So, make sure your treasurer is keeping proper documentation

136
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:35,620
and use the business office to request your balance

137
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:38,620
as a check and a balance, if that makes sense.

138
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:43,900
Student Government Association, one of the functions

139
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:46,900
of your SGA is actually to allocate funds

140
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:49,900
for student organizations.

141
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:52,900
Three things you must do in order to qualify for COA.

142
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:57,900
You must attend and complete RSO training.

143
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:01,900
This semester is actually held in the fall.

144
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:06,900
Going forward, the training will be held in the spring.

145
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:09,900
So, if you get an email from me later this year,

146
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:12,900
beginning up next year, saying it's time for RSO training,

147
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:16,900
I know that we will just head it,

148
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:19,900
but my goal is to get you back on track

149
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:23,900
and to align you with the actual budget processes

150
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:24,900
of student affairs.

151
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:28,900
So, to reiterate, you must complete training,

152
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:31,900
you must submit a budget request form,

153
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:34,900
and you must also go through the RSO recognition period

154
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:38,900
by submitting those documents that we spoke about earlier.

155
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:42,900
The advisor intent form, drug and alcohol-free forms,

156
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:46,900
the roster, all of those documents,

157
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:49,900
those three things comprise the necessary steps

158
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:52,900
you need to do in order to qualify for COA.

159
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:55,900
We're going to talk about the financial processes.

160
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:58,900
I just want to reiterate once more

161
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:03,900
that all agency account transactions for RSOs

162
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:06,900
are submitted through the business office.

163
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:09,900
This does include deposits and new accounts

164
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:16,160
or discussion topics coming up.

165
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:19,160
Agency accounts, transaction types,

166
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:22,160
deposits, and commonly used terms.

167
00:12:24,430 --> 00:12:27,430
What does an agency account actually do for an RSO?

168
00:12:27,430 --> 00:12:30,430
It allows you to check certain functions,

169
00:12:30,430 --> 00:12:33,430
i.e., check the account balance,

170
00:12:33,430 --> 00:12:36,430
make deposits, pay invoices, request funds,

171
00:12:36,430 --> 00:12:39,430
and submit reimbursement vouchers.

172
00:12:39,430 --> 00:12:44,430
You must have an approved agency account on file

173
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:47,430
and approved by the Office of Student Affairs

174
00:12:47,430 --> 00:12:50,430
prior to transactions being processed.

175
00:12:50,430 --> 00:12:56,430
There's nothing that is more discouraging

176
00:12:56,430 --> 00:12:59,430
than to receive a bill for payment

177
00:12:59,430 --> 00:13:03,430
for an outside vendor for X amount of dollars

178
00:13:03,430 --> 00:13:06,430
and there's no agency account to pay for those funds.

179
00:13:06,430 --> 00:13:09,430
So be sure you have your agency account

180
00:13:09,430 --> 00:13:12,430
open and approved by Student Affairs

181
00:13:12,430 --> 00:13:14,430
for conducting any fundraisers.

182
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:19,450
I'd like to complete the form for an agency account

183
00:13:19,450 --> 00:13:24,450
that is actually found online at www.nga.com

184
00:13:24,450 --> 00:13:28,450
slash accounting hyphen services slash docs

185
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:33,450
slash agency underscore account underscore information.

186
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:37,450
That form is also found on the student life documents page.

187
00:13:37,450 --> 00:13:41,020
We're going to talk about reimbursements.

188
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:44,020
Reimbursements for students, faculty, staff,

189
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:46,020
information about travel.

190
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:49,020
There's a new document as it relates to travel

191
00:13:49,020 --> 00:13:51,020
for recognized student organizations.

192
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:53,020
We're going to talk a little bit more about funding

193
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:55,020
and payments for services.

194
00:13:55,020 --> 00:14:00,870
Reimbursement payments for purchases.

195
00:14:00,870 --> 00:14:03,870
This does include students, faculty, and staff.

196
00:14:03,870 --> 00:14:07,870
Reimbursements can be made only under the following conditions.

197
00:14:07,870 --> 00:14:09,870
An individual has paid for something

198
00:14:09,870 --> 00:14:13,870
on behalf of the organization and needs a reimbursement.

199
00:14:13,870 --> 00:14:17,870
The original receipt has been provided.

200
00:14:17,870 --> 00:14:20,870
The purchase was authorized by the RSO

201
00:14:20,870 --> 00:14:22,870
according to meeting minutes.

202
00:14:22,870 --> 00:14:26,870
The RSO has proper funds, agency, or co-op

203
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:28,870
to pay for this voucher.

204
00:14:28,870 --> 00:14:33,470
Students, reimbursements.

205
00:14:33,470 --> 00:14:35,470
Things to remember.

206
00:14:35,470 --> 00:14:39,470
Please do not highlight your items on your receipt

207
00:14:39,470 --> 00:14:41,470
because it makes it very difficult to read

208
00:14:41,470 --> 00:14:43,470
rather than highlight.

209
00:14:43,470 --> 00:14:46,470
Please circle the items that you are referencing

210
00:14:46,470 --> 00:14:47,470
on your receipt.

211
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:51,470
Write your name, your MGA ID number,

212
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:55,470
your RSO name, and your correct mailing address

213
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:56,470
on the receipt.

214
00:14:56,470 --> 00:14:58,470
And just the shameless plug.

215
00:14:58,470 --> 00:15:02,470
You'll see those later on.

216
00:15:02,470 --> 00:15:04,470
But please make sure that your address

217
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:07,470
in Banner is up to date and current

218
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:10,470
because as we begin programming

219
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:13,470
and sending things to you via US Mail,

220
00:15:13,470 --> 00:15:16,470
we want those items to actually make it to you,

221
00:15:16,470 --> 00:15:17,470
make it to your hands.

222
00:15:17,470 --> 00:15:20,470
So make sure that your address in Banner is correct.

223
00:15:20,470 --> 00:15:24,470
Make sure the address of your receipt is also correct.

224
00:15:24,470 --> 00:15:28,470
Receipts must be original, include the date and the total,

225
00:15:28,470 --> 00:15:31,470
be in good condition, and be submitted

226
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:33,470
within two weeks of purchase.

227
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:39,470
We cannot, we cannot reimburse a receipt that's illegible.

228
00:15:39,470 --> 00:15:43,470
You walk around with it in your pocket for a few weeks.

229
00:15:43,470 --> 00:15:46,470
You wash those pants, and then you bring the receipt

230
00:15:46,470 --> 00:15:48,470
to the office to get reimbursed.

231
00:15:48,470 --> 00:15:51,470
If I can't read it, the business office can't read it.

232
00:15:51,470 --> 00:15:54,470
If the business office cannot read your receipt,

233
00:15:54,470 --> 00:15:56,470
there is a very strong likelihood

234
00:15:56,470 --> 00:15:59,470
that you are not going to be able to get a reimbursement

235
00:15:59,470 --> 00:16:00,470
for your purchase.

236
00:16:00,470 --> 00:16:03,470
So submit it in a timely manner,

237
00:16:03,470 --> 00:16:05,470
specifically within two weeks.

238
00:16:05,470 --> 00:16:10,470
Do not mix your personal items with your RSO items

239
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:12,470
in the single transaction.

240
00:16:12,470 --> 00:16:15,470
Rather, separate the transactions.

241
00:16:15,470 --> 00:16:18,470
So we're not looking at your reimbursement receipt

242
00:16:18,470 --> 00:16:22,470
wondering why you may have purchased alcohol

243
00:16:22,470 --> 00:16:28,470
or why you may have purchased potatoes, cereal, milk.

244
00:16:28,470 --> 00:16:30,470
Keep those items very separate

245
00:16:30,470 --> 00:16:33,470
so it's easy to tell from an auditing standpoint

246
00:16:33,470 --> 00:16:36,470
exactly which items offer the RSO.

247
00:16:36,470 --> 00:16:40,470
So on your receipt, just include those RSO items.

248
00:16:40,470 --> 00:16:44,470
Faculty and staff, you will need to enter your reimbursement

249
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:46,470
through the travel and expense module

250
00:16:46,470 --> 00:16:48,470
before payment can be made.

251
00:16:48,470 --> 00:16:52,470
Also, a word of caution about reimbursements.

252
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:56,470
Before any reimbursement can be initiated,

253
00:16:56,470 --> 00:17:01,470
a vendor form, not a W-9, must be on file.

254
00:17:01,470 --> 00:17:04,470
So if you bring the documents in for reimbursement,

255
00:17:04,470 --> 00:17:07,470
we're going to ask you if you've submitted a vendor form.

256
00:17:07,470 --> 00:17:09,470
The good thing about the vendor form is

257
00:17:09,470 --> 00:17:12,470
you only need to do it once.

258
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:14,470
Once you're in our shared system in Sandersville,

259
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:17,470
you no longer have to complete the vendor form.

260
00:17:17,470 --> 00:17:22,620
Reimbursement payments for travel.

261
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:24,620
For students, faculty, and staff,

262
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:28,620
the following conditions must be met prior to traveling

263
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:31,620
and submitting a said reimbursement.

264
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:36,620
There must be a travel authorization request on file.

265
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:41,620
This form is brand new, as of about two weeks ago.

266
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:44,620
So it's very important that you complete the form.

267
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:46,620
It's a very easy form to use.

268
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:48,620
It's a fillable form.

269
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,620
You fill it out online, hits event,

270
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:54,620
and it goes directly to the Vice President of Student Affairs

271
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:58,620
who will verify whether or not he actually have the funds

272
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:00,620
to take this trip.

273
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:05,620
So if you're planning a rather large trip to, say,

274
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:09,620
Disney World and you submit your travel authorization request

275
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:14,620
to Student Affairs for, say, $600 to go to Disney,

276
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:17,620
she's going to check your account and tell you

277
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:20,620
either yes, you can go or no, you cannot go,

278
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:26,620
especially if you only have $5 or that $600 trip to Disney.

279
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,620
Travel documents, which are now only two page,

280
00:18:29,620 --> 00:18:33,620
cut back from four, this does include the travel roster,

281
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:38,620
and it must be on file at least five days before travel occurs.

282
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:40,620
We need those original receipts.

283
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:42,620
I cannot stress that enough.

284
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:47,620
The travel was authorized according to your RSO's meeting minutes.

285
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:49,620
You have the funds to pay for it,

286
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:53,620
and the individual has traveled on behalf of the organization

287
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:57,620
and needs a reimbursement for expenses related to travel.

288
00:18:57,620 --> 00:19:01,860
Travel information for students.

289
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:03,860
Helpful hints.

290
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:07,860
MGA students seeking reimbursement for travel

291
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:10,860
must have travel documents on file.

292
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:15,860
Travel must be approved using the travel authorization request.

293
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:18,860
Travel must be approved by the Office of the Vice President

294
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:20,860
for Student Affairs.

295
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:23,860
MGA faculty and staff will need to enter the reimbursement

296
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:27,860
in the travel and expense module, also known as T&E,

297
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:29,860
before payment can be made.

298
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:32,860
Again, travel must be pre-approved

299
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:35,860
by the Office of the Vice President for Student Affairs.

300
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:39,860
Receipts must include the date and total

301
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:43,860
being good condition, not highlighted, rather,

302
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:46,860
circle the items on the receipt if needed.

303
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:48,860
Must be the original receipts.

304
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:50,860
And again, stressing again,

305
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:55,860
do not mix personal transactions with official transactions.

306
00:19:55,860 --> 00:19:59,860
I've included the link to the MGA travel website,

307
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:03,860
which is www.mga.com,

308
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:07,860
slash accounting, hyphen services, slash travel.

309
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:12,100
Payment methods.

310
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:16,100
Faculty and staff, we will deposit your reimbursements

311
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:19,100
into your checking account,

312
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:21,100
the same as your payroll.

313
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:25,100
For students, your reimbursements will be mailed to you.

314
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:29,100
Again, provide your student ID number,

315
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:34,100
your RSM name, and your correct mailing address.

316
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,100
Because if you're waiting for a reimbursement

317
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:38,100
for a couple of hundred dollars,

318
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,100
you really want to make sure you get that money back

319
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:42,100
as quickly as possible, which is why it's critical

320
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:45,100
that we have your correct mailing address.

321
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:50,180
I just wanted to share with you a couple of commonly used terms.

322
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:53,180
Not everyone might be familiar with these terms.

